# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Café y Tertulias — environment variables (template)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the real values.
# Server-only secrets must NEVER be committed; this file is public.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Where the values come from:
#   • supabase start             → prints the local URL + keys.
#   • supabase status            → shows the current local stack state.
#   • Supabase dashboard (cloud) → Project Settings → API.
#   • vercel env pull .env.local → pulls env from your Vercel project.
#
# Anything prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is shipped to the browser bundle and is
# public by design. Server-only keys must NOT have that prefix.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ─── Supabase (browser + server) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase project URL. Points to the local stack (`supabase start`) in dev,
# to your cloud project in prod. Public — sent to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# Publishable key (formerly "anon key"). Public — sent to the browser.
# Required for the browser/server/proxy Supabase clients; under RLS it only
# exposes what the current user is allowed to see.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=


# ─── Supabase (server-only secret) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret key (formerly "service_role key"). SERVER ONLY — bypasses RLS.
# Used by the admin client to invite members, run admin tasks, and by the
# integration tests to arrange state. NEVER ship this to the client.
#
# If your project still uses the old naming, set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# instead — `lib/supabase/admin.ts` accepts it as a fallback.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=


# ─── Public site URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public origin used in invite / password-reset emails. `lib/site-url.ts`
# falls back to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, then VERCEL_URL, then
# http://127.0.0.1:3000 if unset. GoTrue treats a bare host as invalid and
# will fall back to the project's Site URL (often localhost), so prefer the
# absolute form (with `https://`).
#
# Local: http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Prod:  https://cafe-y-tertulia.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000


# ─── E2E tests (Playwright) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials of the member that runs the "create session → enter Room →
# close it" flow. If left blank, `e2e/session-lifecycle.spec.ts` falls back
# to the values hardcoded in the spec — only useful in CI or on the
# original author's machine.
E2E_EMAIL=
E2E_PASSWORD=

# Override the base URL Playwright targets. Defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:3000 (and Playwright will boot a dev/start server for
# you if this is unset). Set it to a Vercel preview URL or an already
# running server to skip the local boot.
PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=

# Port the local dev/start server listens on when Playwright boots it.
# Matches `next dev --port ${PORT}`. Defaults to 3000.
PORT=3000


# ─── Vercel-provided (do not set by hand) ──────────────────────────────────
# Vercel injects these automatically at runtime — you don't need to define
# them in `.env.local`. Listed here only because `lib/site-url.ts` reads
# them as a fallback when NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is missing.
#
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL  → host of the production branch
# VERCEL_URL                     → host of the current deployment (preview or prod)
